Many statements crammed onto single lines, including block openers and
closers sharing a line with body statements. The formatter's handling of
statements per line is recorded here (one per line, or kept), and the
indentation must still follow the block structure.
-- input.ssl --
:PROCEDURE Crammed; :PARAMETERS nA, nB; :DECLARE nSum, sOut; nSum := nA + nB;
:IF nSum > 10; sOut := "big"; :ELSE; sOut := "small"; :ENDIF; :RETURN sOut; :ENDPROC;
-- format --
:PROCEDURE Crammed;
	:PARAMETERS nA, nB;
	:DECLARE nSum, sOut;
	nSum := nA + nB;
	:IF nSum > 10;
		sOut := "big";
	:ELSE;
		sOut := "small";
	:ENDIF;
	:RETURN sOut;
:ENDPROC;
-- diagnostics --
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
